From karimihussein-Re5JQEeQqe8AvxtiuMwx3w at public.gmane.org  Fri Dec 12 01:22:26 2014
From: karimihussein-Re5JQEeQqe8AvxtiuMwx3w at public.gmane.org (Hossein Karimi)
Date: Thu, 11 Dec 2014 20:22:26 -0500
Subject: Question about bobyga optimizer
Message-ID: <CALiysJRrmjh4Qe+t1-LnJTh8880jGLFy-J3b5SiU8jquBb4hsw@mail.gmail.com>

Hi everyone,

I'm trying to run logit mixed effects models with maximal random effects
structures on my data using "bobyqa" optimizer. The models seem to converge
(after a really long time though!), but I get the following warning message:

Warning messages:
1: In commonArgs(par, fn, control, environment()) :
  maxfun < 10 * length(par)^2 is not recommended.
2: In commonArgs(par, fn, control, environment()) :
  maxfun < 10 * length(par)^2 is not recommended.


Does this mean the model needs more iterations? If yes, how can I allow
that?

Or, should I just simplify the random effects structure?

Many thanks,

Hossein

From danielezrajohnson-Re5JQEeQqe8AvxtiuMwx3w at public.gmane.org  Fri Dec 12 06:53:42 2014
From: danielezrajohnson-Re5JQEeQqe8AvxtiuMwx3w at public.gmane.org (Daniel Ezra Johnson)
Date: Fri, 12 Dec 2014 06:53:42 +0000
Subject: Re: Question about bobyga optimizer
In-Reply-To: <CALiysJRrmjh4Qe+t1-LnJTh8880jGLFy-J3b5SiU8jquBb4hsw@mail.gmail.com>
References: <CALiysJRrmjh4Qe+t1-LnJTh8880jGLFy-J3b5SiU8jquBb4hsw@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <CAABSvoUmd6mT1MoNoyhriK6Ty2WpDX07271yy64RNr28Gq_igg@mail.gmail.com>

Dear Hossein,

You can increase the number of iterations with the lmerControl function,
like this:

m1 <- lmer(y ~ f + (1 | r), data, control = lmerControl(optCtrl = list(
maxfun=100000)))


But as you say, you may want to simplify your model, which seems to have at
least...32 parameters. Or you could do both.


Hope this helps,

Dan

